# Secrets Env Has One Loader

Loading the secrets environment is centralized in the single zsh file that runs for every invocation, interactive or not, login or not. That one file covers macOS and Linux alike, so there is no per-platform loader and no second source site. A separate secrets library file existed once and was deleted in the July 2026 dedupe as redundant.

**Why:** the secrets environment is a cross-platform contract, not a macOS convenience. More than one loader means the environment differs by shell type, and the resulting failures land far from the cause, since a variable present in an interactive shell can be missing in the one an agent actually gets. Confirmed by the owner on 2026-07-20.

**How to apply:** Keep exactly one loader. A new machine of either OS follows the same contract rather than inventing its own location. When something authenticates in your terminal but not under automation, check which shell files each path reads before suspecting the credential. Related: [gh-env-token-auth-is-invisible](mdc:.cursor/rules/gh-env-token-auth-is-invisible.mdc), [secrets-writes-dotenvx-only](mdc:.cursor/rules/secrets-writes-dotenvx-only.mdc).
